\\\"},{\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Fund arrangements are outside the selected LC control and retained as context.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"CONTEXT\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u8.2499\\\"},{\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Fund alerts and remedial action are outside the selected LC control and retained as context.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"CONTEXT\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u9.2771\\\"},{\\\"reason\\\":\\\"SFC monitoring is contextual dependency information, not an LC condition.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"CONTEXT\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u10.2996\\\"},{\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Issuing department attribution is contextual scope information.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"CONTEXT\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u11.3083\\\"},{\\\"reason\\\":\\\"SFC institutional attribution is contextual scope information.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"CONTEXT\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u12.3172\\\"},{\\\"reason\\\":\\\"SFC attribution is contextual scope information.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"CONTEXT\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u13.3290\\\"},{\\\"reason\\\":\\\"The illustrative securities examples qualify the scope of US securities.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"INTERPRETED\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u14.3336\\\"},{\\\"reason\\\":\\\"The Canada date and definition of Transition are interpreted as scope and time qualifications.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"INTERPRETED\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u15.3399\\\"},{\\\"reason\\\":\\\"The meaning of post-trade settlement processes is used in the completion fact.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"INTERPRETED\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u16.3567\\\"}],\\\"dimensions\\\":[{\\\"dimension\\\":\\\"scope\\\",\\\"explanation\\\":\\\"The selected control concerns licensed corporations. Fund-management provisions and SFC monitoring remain contextual. The Transition is defined to include the US and Canada, while several operational examples expressly refer to US securities.\\\",\\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u0.0\\\",\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u1.498\\\",\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u6.2116\\\",\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u14.3336\\\",\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u15.3399\\\"],\\\"status\\\":\\\"PROPOSED\\\"},{\\\"dimension\\\":\\\"definitions\\\",\\\"explanation\\\":\\\"The Transition comprises the US and Canadian T+1 changes; post-trade settlement processes include trade allocation, confirmation and affirmation. The securities list is illustrative rather than exhaustive.\\\",\\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u0.0\\\",\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u14.3336\\\",\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u15.3399\\\",\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u16.3567\\\"],\\\"status\\\":\\\"PROPOSED\\\"},{\\\"dimension\\\":\\\"exceptions\\\",\\\"explanation\\\":\\\"Staffing enhancements are qualified by appropriateness in the general reminder; scheduling, extended hours and automation are optional considerations. Fund arrangements are separate and conditional. Cross-currency mismatch language applies only to cross-currency transactions.\\\",\\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u1.498\\\",\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u3.996\\\",\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u4.1448\\\",\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u8.2499\\\"],\\\"status\\\":\\\"AMBIGUOUS\\\"},{\\\"dimension\\\":\\\"modality\\\",\\\"explanation\\\":\\\"The source uses should for readiness, funding, staffing, training and client engagement, and may for particular scheduling and automation methods. It does not expressly state must, leaving unresolved whether every listed item is independently required.\\\",\\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u1.498\\\",\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u2.879\\\",\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u3.996\\\",\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u4.1448\\\",\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u5.1916\\\"],\\\"status\\\":\\\"AMBIGUOUS\\\"},{\\\"dimension\\\":\\\"time\\\",\\\"explanation\\\":\\\"US settlement changes to T+1 on 2024-05-28; Canada changes on 2024-05-27. Readiness concerns the shortened timeframe and operations after the Transition, but no separate assessment or training deadline is stated.\\\",\\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u0.0\\\",\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u1.498\\\",\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u4.1448\\\",\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u15.3399\\\"],\\\"status\\\":\\\"PROPOSED\\\"},{\\\"dimension\\\":\\\"dependencies\\\",\\\"explanation\\\":\\\"Cross-currency readiness depends on the foreign-exchange cycle remaining T+2 and on avoiding liquidity mismatches or settlement failures. SFC monitoring is contextual rather than a condition of LC compliance.\\\",\\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u3.996\\\",\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u10.2996\\\"],\\\"status\\\":\\\"PROPOSED\\\"}],\\\"questions\\\":[\\\"Does “including” make each listed readiness item independently expected, or are they examples of measures supporting the broader ability-to-cope outcome?\\\",\\\"Is client engagement required for every LC or only when a client is potentially affected?\\\",\\\"What evidence establishes that cross-currency T+2 mismatch and settlement-failure risks have been addressed?\\\",\\\"Does the Transition definition extend every US-specific control to Canada, or only references using the defined term Transition?\\\"],\\\"readings\\\":[{\\\"assumptions\\\":[\\\"The selected control is an LC operational-readiness outcome, not a certification that every listed method was used.\\\",\\\"Unknown facts remain unknown.\\\",\\\"Client engagement is assessed only where clients are potentially affected.\\\"],\\\"citations\\\":[{\\\"quote\\\":\\\"LCs should assess their readiness and ensure they are able to cope with the shortened settlement cycle, including:\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u2.879\\\"},{\\\"quote\\\":\\\"Ensuring the availability of staff to complete the post-trade settlement processes within the shortened timeframe.\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u4.1448\\\"},{\\\"quote\\\":\\\"Proactively engaging and communicating with their clients who are potentially affected by the Transition in order to raise their awareness and facilitate their preparations for a smooth transition.\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u5.1916\\\"},{\\\"quote\\\":\\\"LCs may consider adjusting their staff’s work shifts, extending working hours or arranging evening or morning duties in conjunction with automating their operational processes to enable timely trade settlements.\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u4.1448\\\"}],\\\"distinction\\\":\\\"Reading A treats “including” as introducing representative controls supporting the overarching outcome: the LC has assessed readiness and can cope with the shortened cycle. The optional scheduling and automation measures are methods, not mandatory elements. Liquidity, staffing and training evidence informs whether the outcome is achieved, while client engagement applies when clients are potentially affected.\\\",\\\"family\\\":\\\"exceptions\\\",\\\"formalization\\\":{\\\"facts\\\":[{\\\"meaning\\\":\\\"The LC has assessed the Transition’s impact on its business and readiness.\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"lc_readiness_assessed\\\",\\\"requires_judgment\\\":true,\\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u1.498\\\",\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u2.879\\\"],\\\"type\\\":\\\"bool\\\",\\\"unit\\\":\\\"boolean\\\"},{\\\"meaning\\\":\\\"The LC can complete trade allocation, confirmation, affirmation and other relevant post-trade settlement processes within the shortened timeframe.\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"lc_can_complete_post_trade_on_time\\\",\\\"requires_judgment\\\":true,\\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u2.879\\\",\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u4.1448\\\",\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u16.3567\\\"],\\\"type\\\":\\\"bool\\\",\\\"unit\\\":\\\"boolean\\\"},{\\\"meaning\\\":\\\"The LC has reviewed liquidity-risk practices and has necessary funding for timely US-securities settlement, including consideration of cross-currency mismatch risk where relevant.\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"lc_liquidity_and_funding_ready\\\",\\\"requires_judgment\\\":true,\\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u3.996\\\"],\\\"type\\\":\\\"bool\\\",\\\"unit\\\":\\\"boolean\\\"},{\\\"meaning\\\":\\\"The LC has staff availability and adequate training for duties under the shortened cycle.\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"lc_staffing_and_training_ready\\\",\\\"requires_judgment\\\":true,\\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u4.1448\\\"],\\\"type\\\":\\\"bool\\\",\\\"unit\\\":\\\"boolean\\\"},{\\\"meaning\\\":\\\"The LC has engaged clients potentially affected by the Transition sufficiently to raise awareness and facilitate preparation.\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"lc_client_engagement_completed\\\",\\\"requires_judgment\\\":true,\\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u5.1916\\\"],\\\"type\\\":\\\"bool\\\",\\\"unit\\\":\\\"boolean\\\"}],\\\"result\\\":\\\"(and lc_readiness_assessed lc_can_complete_post_trade_on_time lc_liquidity_and_funding_ready lc_staffing_and_training_ready lc_client_engagement_completed)\\\",\\\"result_type\\\":\\\"bool\\\",\\\"scope\\\":\\\"Selected LC operational-readiness control for the Transition, with client engagement required when clients are potentially affected.\\\"},\\\"local_id\\\":\\\"reading_a\\\",\\\"questions\\\":[\\\"What objective evidence demonstrates the LC can cope with the shortened cycle without adopting any particular staffing method?\\\",\\\"How should the potentially affected-client condition be determined?\\\"],\\\"statement\\\":\\\"[TRUE_IS_COMPLIANT] The selected LC readiness control is compliant when the LC has assessed impact and readiness, can complete post-trade settlement on time, has reviewed liquidity and funding, has adequate staff and training, and has communicated with potentially affected clients.\\\" ,\\\"subject\\\":\\\"Licensed corporation operational readiness\\\"},{\\\"assumptions\\\":[\\\"Each listed readiness item introduced under “including” is treated as a separate expected control.\\\",\\\"The optional scheduling and automation sentence remains permissive and is not itself required.\\\",\\\"Client engagement is required when the LC has potentially affected clients.\\\"],\\\"citations\\\":[{\\\"quote\\\":\\\"LCs should assess their readiness and ensure they are able to cope with the shortened settlement cycle, including:\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u2.879\\\"},{\\\"quote\\\":\\\"Reviewing their liquidity risk management practices and ensuring the necessary funding is available for settling US securities transactions on time.\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u3.996\\\"},{\\\"quote\\\":\\\"Adequate training should be provided to enable relevant staff to effectively perform their duties under the shortened settlement cycle; and\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u4.1448\\\"},{\\\"quote\\\":\\\"These include enhancing their operational processes, technological infrastructure and systems as well as staffing arrangements where appropriate.\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u1.498\\\"}],\\\"distinction\\\":\\\"Reading B treats the readiness outcome and each enumerated “should” item as cumulative controls: failure of any applicable liquidity/funding, staff availability, training, or client-engagement control means the selected control is not compliant. “Where appropriate,” “potentially affected,” and the cross-currency qualifier limit applicability, while the may sentence preserves discretion over particular staffing methods.\\\",\\\"family\\\":\\\"modality\\\",\\\"formalization\\\":{\\\"facts\\\":[{\\\"meaning\\\":\\\"The LC has assessed the Transition’s impact on its business and readiness.\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"lc_readiness_assessed\\\",\\\"requires_judgment\\\":true,\\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u1.498\\\",\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u2.879\\\"],\\\"type\\\":\\\"bool\\\",\\\"unit\\\":\\\"boolean\\\"},{\\\"meaning\\\":\\\"The LC can complete relevant post-trade settlement processes within the shortened timeframe.\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"lc_can_complete_post_trade_on_time\\\",\\\"requires_judgment\\\":true,\\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u2.879\\\",\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u4.1448\\\",\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u16.3567\\\"],\\\"type\\\":\\\"bool\\\",\\\"unit\\\":\\\"boolean\\\"},{\\\"meaning\\\":\\\"The LC has reviewed liquidity-risk practices and necessary funding for timely US-securities settlement.\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"lc_liquidity_and_funding_ready\\\",\\\"requires_judgment\\\":true,\\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u3.996\\\"],\\\"type\\\":\\\"bool\\\",\\\"unit\\\":\\\"boolean\\\"},{\\\"meaning\\\":\\\"The LC has staff available and has provided adequate training for relevant duties.\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"lc_staffing_and_training_ready\\\",\\\"requires_judgment\\\":true,\\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u4.1448\\\"],\\\"type\\\":\\\"bool\\\",\\\"unit\\\":\\\"boolean\\\"},{\\\"meaning\\\":\\\"The LC has proactively engaged potentially affected clients to raise awareness and facilitate preparation.\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"lc_client_engagement_completed\\\",\\\"requires_judgment\\\":true,\\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"d2ccfaeb3eb4b.u5.1916\\\"],\\\"type\\\":\\\"bool\\\",\\\"unit\\\":\\\"boolean\\\"}],\\\"result\\\":\\\"(and lc_readiness_assessed lc_can_complete_post_trade_on_time lc_liquidity_and_funding_ready lc_staffing_and_training_ready lc_client_engagement_completed)\\\",\\\"result_type\\\":\\\"bool\\\",\\\"scope\\\":\\\"Selected cumulative LC controls for operational readiness under the Transition; particular scheduling or automation methods remain optional.\\\"},\\\"local_id\\\":\\\"reading_b\\\",\\\"questions\\\":[\\\"Does the “including” list exhaust the minimum readiness controls or merely illustrate them?\\\",\\\"When is a staffing arrangement “appropriate,” and who determines that?\\\",\\\"Are Canadian transactions included in each US-securities-specific funding control?\\\"],\\\"statement\\\":\\\"[TRUE_IS_COMPLIANT] The selected control is compliant only when the LC has completed the readiness assessment and each applicable listed control for timely settlement, liquidity and funding, staffing and training, and communication with potentially affected clients.\\\" ,\\\"subject\\\":\\\"Licensed corporation cumulative readiness controls\\\"}]}\"}}\n{\"type\":\"turn.comp